        <p><strong>Storm damage leads</strong> are the highest-value, fastest-closing leads in roofing. Twenty-two percent of all roofing projects originate from storm damage, and 12 million properties were hit by hail in 2024 alone. <strong>Replacement leads</strong> are the bread and butter — 44% of U.S. single-family homes are 30+ years old, and 63.5% of market revenue comes from re-roofing. <strong>Repair leads</strong> close the fastest at 40–60% but have the lowest ticket size.</p>

        <h3>The Roofing Revenue Cycle</h3>
        <p>Here is how the cycle works: <strong>Attract</strong> (homeowner becomes aware they need roofing) → <strong>Search</strong> (they look for contractors) → <strong>Evaluate</strong> (they compare 2–4 contractors) → <strong>Convert</strong> (they book an inspection) → <strong>Deliver</strong> (you complete the job) → <strong>Amplify</strong> (satisfied customer refers others). The best roofing companies optimize every stage — not just lead generation.</p>

        <h2>Chapter 1: Building Your Roofing Marketing Foundation</h2>
        <p>Before you run a single ad or write a blog post, you need a foundation. Most roofing companies skip this step and wonder why their marketing feels scattered.</p>

        <h3>Define Your Ideal Customer</h3>
        <p>Roofing is not one market. It is at least four: residential replacement, residential repair, storm damage restoration, and commercial. Each requires different messaging, different pricing, and different marketing channels. A storm damage specialist in Dallas needs a completely different marketing system than a luxury residential roofer in Scottsdale.</p>

        <h3>Develop Your Unique Selling Proposition (USP)</h3>
        <p>Homeowners cannot tell the difference between roofers. Your USP is what makes you the obvious choice.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Instead of <em>"Quality workmanship"</em> → <strong>"We complete 95% of jobs in one day"</strong></li>
          <li>Instead of <em>"Licensed and insured"</em> → <strong>"Licensed in 3 states with $2M liability coverage"</strong></li>
          <li>Instead of <em>"Free estimates"</em> → <strong>"Free drone inspection + same-day written estimate"</strong></li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Set Your Service Area Strategy</h3>
        <p>Many roofers claim a 100-mile service radius. That destroys your local SEO and operational efficiency. <strong>Only market to areas where you can complete a job start-to-finish within one day.</strong> That usually means a 20–30 mile radius. For each service area, create a dedicated location page on your website.</p>

