        <h2>Chapter 2: Local SEO for Roofing Companies</h2>
        <p>Local SEO is the single highest-ROI marketing channel for roofing companies. Period. The Local 3-Pack appears in <strong>93% of local searches</strong> and captures 44–50% of all clicks. If you are not in the top three map results for "roofing contractor near me," you are invisible to the majority of your market.</p>

        <h3>Google Business Profile Optimization</h3>
        <p>Your Google Business Profile (GBP) is the single most important digital asset for local SEO. Here is the optimization checklist:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Primary Category:</strong> Must be "Roofing Contractor" (used by 94.3% of top-ranking roofers)</li>
          <li><strong>Secondary Categories:</strong> Add Siding Contractor, Gutter Cleaning Service, Storm Damage Restoration</li>
          <li><strong>Photos:</strong> Upload 10+ high-quality images. Update quarterly. Complete profiles are 70% more likely to attract visits</li>
          <li><strong>Weekly Posts:</strong> Publish every week. Google interprets this as an active, legitimate business</li>
          <li><strong>Services & Attributes:</strong> Add Emergency Service, Free Estimates, Financing Available, Licensed & Insured</li>
          <li><strong>Service Area:</strong> Set a realistic 20–30 mile radius</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Review Generation Systems</h3>
        <p>The data is clear: roofers with <strong>15+ new reviews per month earn 3x more calls</strong>. A roofer with 60 reviews at 4.8 stars typically outranks a competitor with 10 reviews at 5.0 stars.</p>
        <p><strong>Best practices:</strong> Send automated text review requests within 24 hours of job completion. Customers are 42% more likely to respond immediately after a job is finished. Reply to every review — positive and negative — within 48 hours.</p>

        <h3>Location Page Architecture</h3>
        <p>Create dedicated landing pages for every city and neighborhood you serve. Each page should include: city name in H1, title tag, and URL; local roofing challenges specific to that area; 2–3 testimonials from customers in that area; photos of completed jobs; and LocalBusiness schema markup.</p>

        <h3>Local Link Building for Roofers</h3>
        <p>Build local authority through Chamber of Commerce membership, local sports team sponsorships, partnerships with real estate agents, guest posts on local business blogs, and features in local news. Build citations on 50+ directories with identical NAP (Name, Address, Phone) information.</p>

