        <h3>Google Ads Strategy</h3>
        <p>Bid on high-intent, long-tail keywords: <strong>"roof replacement [city]," "emergency roof repair near me," "hail damage roof inspection [city]."</strong> Avoid broad terms like "roofing" or "roofer." Include numbers in ad copy: "15+ Years in [City]" or "Same-Day Inspections."</p>

        <h3>Google Local Services Ads (LSAs)</h3>
        <p>LSAs appear at the top with a "Google Guaranteed" badge. You pay per lead, not per click. However, 67% of contractors say LSA lead quality declined in 2025, and Google removed junk-lead credits. Use LSAs as part of a diversified strategy, not your only channel.</p>

        <h3>Facebook and Instagram Ads</h3>
        <p>Social ads work best for storm damage awareness, brand building, retargeting, and video testimonials. Target homeowners aged 35–65 in your service area with home improvement interests. AI-powered targeting can now micro-target homeowners with aging roofs (15+ years).</p>

        <h3>Lead Aggregator Warning</h3>
        <p>HomeAdvisor, Angi, and Thumbtack sell the same lead to 3–5 contractors. Shared leads close below 10–15% because homeowners default to the lowest price. Exclusive leads from your own website close at 30–50%. Budget no more than 15% of your paid spend on shared leads.</p>

