        <h2>Chapter 6: Referral and Partnership Marketing</h2>
        <p>Referral leads are the highest-quality, lowest-cost leads in roofing. They close at 30–50%+, have the highest lifetime value, and cost only $10–$25 in incentive cost. Yet most roofing companies treat referrals as an afterthought.</p>

        <h3>Insurance Agent Partnerships</h3>
        <p>Insurance agents are your highest-value partners. When a homeowner files a claim, the agent often recommends a roofer. Being that recommended roofer is worth hundreds of thousands annually.</p>
        <p><strong>How to build these relationships:</strong> Identify agents who write homeowner policies in your area. Offer free roof inspections for their clients. Provide educational materials on roofing claims. Give them a one-page "preferred contractor" sheet. Check in quarterly.</p>

        <h3>Real Estate Agent Relationships</h3>
        <p>Real estate agents need roofers for pre-listing inspections, repair credits, and replacement before closing. Partner with top-producing agents. Offer 24-hour inspection turnaround and direct communication with the agent.</p>

        <h3>Customer Referral Programs</h3>
        <p>One Florida roofing company boosted referrals by 40% using gamified referral programs with leaderboards and monthly prizes.</p>
