        <h3>Contractor Referral Networks</h3>
        <p>Build relationships with HVAC contractors, siding and gutter companies, general contractors, and painters. Create a formal referral exchange: you send them leads, they send you leads.</p>

        <h2>Chapter 7: Content Marketing for Roofing Companies</h2>
        <p>Content marketing builds trust before the homeowner ever calls you. In roofing — where the average ticket is $8,000–$15,000 and homeowners fear being ripped off — trust is everything.</p>

        <h3>Blog Topics That Generate Leads</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>"How much does a roof replacement cost in [City]?"</li>
          <li>"How to tell if your roof has hail damage"</li>
          <li>"How long does a roof last?"</li>
          <li>"How to file a roof insurance claim"</li>
          <li>"Roofing contractor vs. storm chaser: how to tell"</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>The Content Multiplication Strategy</h3>
        <p>Most roofing companies create one piece of content and move on. Top performers extract 10+ pieces from every project. <strong>One roof replacement becomes:</strong> a before/after gallery, time-lapse video, blog post, customer testimonial, drone footage, 5–7 social posts, email case study, sales presentation slide, GBP photo update, and Nextdoor post. This reduces content production costs by 30–40%.</p>

        <h3>Video Content</h3>
        <p>Video testimonials (15–30 second clips) outperform text reviews by 300% in engagement. Post educational videos (2–3 minutes) on YouTube, Instagram Reels, TikTok, and Facebook. Film storm damage walkthroughs in storm-hit neighborhoods.</p>

        <h3>Social Media for Roofers</h3>
        <p><strong>Nextdoor</strong> is the most underrated platform for roofers. Active accounts generate 2–3 hyperlocal leads per week at $0 cost. Post about local projects, storm warnings, and educational tips. On Facebook and Instagram, post 3–5 times per week with a mix of educational, proof, and personal content.</p>

        <h3>Email Marketing</h3>
        <p>Your past customers are your warmest audience. Email them seasonally with maintenance reminders, pre-storm inspections, and referral program announcements. Segment your list: past customers, unconverted estimates, website visitors, and commercial contacts.</p>

        <h2>Chapter 8: Tracking, Measurement, and ROI</h2>
        <p>You cannot improve what you do not measure. Most roofing companies track only one metric: how many leads came in this month. That is like driving with only a speedometer.</p>

