        <h3>Call Tracking Setup</h3>
        <p>Many roofing leads call rather than fill out forms. Without call tracking, you do not know which channel generated the call. Implement unique phone numbers for each channel, call recording, missed call alerts, and CRM integration.</p>

        <h3>ROI Calculation Framework</h3>
        <p><strong>ROI = (Revenue from Marketing - Marketing Cost) / Marketing Cost × 100</strong></p>
        <p>Example: $5,000 monthly spend → 50 leads → 20% close rate (10 sales) → $10,000 average ticket → $100,000 revenue → <strong>1,900% ROI</strong>. The advanced metric is <strong>Cost Per Sale by Channel</strong>, not just cost per lead.</p>

        <h2>Chapter 9: The 12 Roofing Marketing Mistakes Costing You $50K+</h2>
        <p>After auditing hundreds of roofing companies' marketing, we see the same mistakes repeatedly.</p>

        <h3>Mistake 1: Relying on a Single Lead Source</h3>
        <p>The roofers who struggle most get 80% of leads from one channel. When that channel dries up, so does revenue. <strong>Fix:</strong> No single channel should contribute more than 40% of your leads.</p>

        <h3>Mistake 2: Sending Paid Traffic to Your Homepage</h3>
        <p>Your homepage is a navigation tool, not a landing page. <strong>Fix:</strong> Build dedicated landing pages for every service and campaign.</p>

        <h3>Mistake 3: Ignoring Mobile Experience</h3>
        <p>61% of roofing searches happen on mobile, yet mobile conversions lag desktop (1.5% vs. 4.1%). <strong>Fix:</strong> Design mobile-first with thumb-sized click-to-call buttons.</p>

        <h3>Mistake 4: Slow Follow-Up</h3>
        <p>The first contractor to respond wins the job ~78% of the time. Delaying by 24 hours drops conversion by 40%. <strong>Fix:</strong> Automated text responses within 60 seconds.</p>

        <h3>Mistake 5: No Review Generation System</h3>
        <p>15+ reviews per month = 3x more calls. <strong>Fix:</strong> Automated text requests within 24 hours of job completion.</p>

        <h3>Mistake 6: Buying Shared Leads Exclusively</h3>
        <p>Shared leads from HomeAdvisor close at 10–15% vs. 30–50% for exclusive leads. <strong>Fix:</strong> Use aggregators as a supplement only (under 15% of paid spend).</p>

        <h3>Mistake 7: No Seasonal Strategy</h3>
        <p>Most roofers market heavily during storm season and go silent in winter. <strong>Fix:</strong> Build a 12-month marketing calendar.</p>

        <h3>Mistake 8: Generic Messaging</h3>
        <p>"Quality workmanship" tells homeowners nothing. <strong>Fix:</strong> Be specific: "We complete 95% of jobs in one day."</p>

        <h3>Mistake 9: No Call Tracking</h3>
        <p>Without tracking, you are flying blind. <strong>Fix:</strong> Unique numbers per channel, reviewed monthly.</p>

        <h3>Mistake 10: Neglecting Past Customers</h3>
        <p>Your past customers already trust you. <strong>Fix:</strong> Email them seasonally with maintenance tips and referral requests.</p>

        <h3>Mistake 11: Using Stock Photos</h3>
        <p>Stock photos tell homeowners you are hiding something. <strong>Fix:</strong> Document every job with real photos and videos.</p>

        <h3>Mistake 12: No Website Conversion Optimization</h3>
        <p>The average roofing website converts at 0.5–2%. Optimized sites reach 8–14.5%. <strong>Fix:</strong> Add estimate tools, CTAs, and trust signals. A/B test continuously.</p>

        <h2>Your 12-Month Roofing Marketing Calendar</h2>
        <p>Roofing is seasonal. Your marketing should be too.</p>

        <h3>Q1: January–March (Slow Season / Preparation)</h3>
        <p><strong>Focus:</strong> Build systems, create content, prepare for storm season.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Week 1: Audit website and GBP; fix technical issues</li>
          <li>Week 2: Create storm landing pages for top 5 service areas</li>
          <li>Week 3: Build email nurture sequences</li>
          <li>Week 4: Film 6 educational videos</li>
        </ul>
